statement.p:
Use graphical and numerical methods to approximate

  \lim_{x\to 3} \frac{x^2-x-6}{6x^2-19x+3}
.

solution.p:
To graphically approximate the limit, graph
y = \frac{x^2-x-6}{6x^2-19x+3}
on a small interval that contains 3. To numerically approximate the limit, create a table of values where the x values are near 3. This is done in and , respectively.

