li.p:
As x approaches  0 from the right, we consider a limit where all x-values are greater than 0.
This means we use the 2-x piece of f. As the x-values near 0, 2-x approaches 2;
that is, f(x) approaches 2.

As x approaches  2 from the left, we consider a limit where all x-values are less than 2.
This means we use the (x-2)^2 piece of f. As the x-values near 2, (x-2)^2 nears 0;
that is, f(x) approaches 0.

