subsection.p:
What we are really computing is the average velocity on the interval [2,2+h] for small values of h. That is, we are computing
\frac{f(2+h) - f(2)}{h}
where h is small.

Computing the limit directly gives

  \lim_{h\to 0} \frac{f(2+h)-f(2)}{h} \amp = \lim_{h\to 0}\frac{-16(2+h)^2+150 -   (-16(2)^2+150)}{h}
  \amp = \lim_{h\to 0}\frac{-16(4+4h+h^2)+150 - 86}{h}
  \amp = \lim_{h\to 0}\frac{-64-64h-16h^2+64}{h}
  \amp = \lim_{h\to 0}\frac{-64h-16h^2}{h}
  \amp = \lim_{h\to 0}(-64 -16h)
  \amp =-64
.

