solution.p:
To find the appropriate slopes of tangent lines to the graph of f,
we need to look at the corresponding values of \fp.





      The slope of the tangent line to f at x=1 is \fp(1);
      this looks to be about -1.






      The slope of the tangent line to f at x=2 is \fp(2);
      this looks to be about 4.






      The slope of the tangent line to f at x=3 is \fp(3);
      this looks to be about 3.

