section.p:
Let's abstract once more.
Let's find the derivative of the general quadratic function,
f(x) = ax^2+bx+c.
Using the definition of the derivative, we have:

  \fp(x) \amp = \lim_{h\to 0}\frac{a(x+h)^2+b(x+h)+c-(ax^2+bx+c)}{h}
  \amp = \lim_{h\to 0}\frac{ax^2+2ahx+ah^2+bx+bh+c-ax^2-bx-c}{h}
  \amp = \lim_{h\to 0} \frac{ah^2+2ahx+bh}{h}
  \amp = \lim_{h\to 0} ah+2ax+b
  \amp = 2ax+b
.

