solution.p:
Factor out \yp from the left side and solve to get

  \yp = \frac{2-2xy^4}{3y^2+4x^2y^3}
.

From here we can safely move around terms to get the following:

  2x^2y\cos\mathopen{}\left(x^2y^2\right)\mathclose{}\yp + 3y^2\yp - \yp = 1 - 2xy^2\cos\mathopen{}\left(x^2y^2\right)\mathclose{}
.

Then we can solve for \yp to get

  \yp = \frac{1 - 2xy^2\cos\mathopen{}\left(x^2y^2\right)\mathclose{}}{2x^2y\cos\mathopen{}\left(x^2y^2\right)\mathclose{}+3y^2-1}
.

