solution.p:
To find the slope of the astroid at the point (8,8),
we take the derivative implicitly.

  \frac{2}{3}x^{-1/3}+\frac{2}{3}y^{-1/3}\yp\amp =0
  \frac{2}{3}y^{-1/3}\yp \amp = -\frac{2}{3}x^{-1/3}
  \yp\amp =-\frac{x^{-1/3}}{y^{-1/3}}
  \yp\amp =-\frac{y^{1/3}}{x^{1/3}} = -\sqrt[3]{\frac{y}{x}}
.

