statement.p:
Let f be differentiable and one-to-one on an open interval I,
where \fp(x) \neq 0 for all x in I,
let J be the range of f on I,
let g be the inverse function of f,
and let f(a) = b for some a in I.
Then g is a differentiable function on J,
and in particular,




    \left(f^{-1}\right)'(b)=\gp(b) = \dfrac{1}{\fp(a)}




    \left(f^{-1}\right)'(x)=\gp(x) = \dfrac{1}{\fp(g(x))}

