statement.p:
        The inverse trigonometric functions are differentiable on all open sets contained in their domains
        (as listed in )
        and their derivatives are as follows:



\lzoo{x}{\sin^{-1}(x)} = \frac{1}{\sqrt{1-x^2}}


\lzoo{x}{\cos^{-1}(x)} = -\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-x^2}}


\lzoo{x}{\tan^{-1}(x)} = \frac{1}{1+x^2}


\lzoo{x}{\csc^{-1}(x)} = -\frac{1}{\abs{x}\sqrt{x^2-1}}


\lzoo{x}{\sec^{-1}(x)} = \frac{1}{\abs{x}\sqrt{x^2-1}}


\lzoo{x}{\cot^{-1}(x)} = -\frac{1}{1+x^2}


        derivativeinverse trig.

solution.p:
View y= \ln(x) as the inverse of y = e^x.
Therefore, using our standard notation,
let f(x) = e^x and g(x) = \ln(x).
We wish to find \gp(x).
 gives:

  \gp(x) \amp = \frac{1}{\fp(g(x))}
  \amp = \frac{1}{e^{\ln(x) }}
  \amp = \frac{1}{x}
.

