statement.p:
Find the maximum and minimum values of f on [-4,2], where

  f(x) = \begin{cases}(x-1)^2 \amp  x\leq 0 \\ x+1 \amp  x \gt 0\end{cases}
.

solution.p:
Note that while f is defined for all of [-4,2],
\fp is not,
as the derivative of f does not exist when x=0.
(From the left, the derivative approaches -2;
from the right the derivative is 1.)
Thus one critical number of f is x=0.

