li.p:
Choose any two points a and b in the interval I. By the Mean Value Theorem, we must have
\fp(c) = \frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}
for some c between a and b. But \fp(c)=0, so f(b)-f(a)=0, or f(a)=f(b). Since a and b were any two points, this tells us that f must have the same value at every point; that is, f must be constant.

