solution.p:
Using the , we find

  \fp(x) = \frac{x^2-2x-3}{(x-1)^2}
.

\fp(x)=0 when the numerator of \fp(x) is 0.
That occurs when x^2-2x-3 = (x-3)(x+1) = 0;
, when x=-1,3.

