subsection.p:
Recall that relative maxima and minima of f are found at critical points of f;
that is, they are found when
\fp(x)=0 or when \fp is undefined.
Likewise, the relative maxima and minima of  \fp are found when
\fpp(x)=0 or when  \fpp is undefined;
note that these are the inflection points of f.

