solution.p:
Taking the derivative of (\cosh x)^2 directly,
one gets 2\cosh x\sinh x;
using the identity \cosh^2x=\frac12(\cosh2x+1) first,
one gets \sinh 2x;
by known hyperbolic identities,
these are equal.

subsection.p:
We demonstrate the use of l'Hospital's Rule in the following examples;
we will often use LHR as an abbreviation of
l'Hospital's Rule.

