solution.p:
The conical tank is sketched in .
We can orient the tank in a variety of ways;
we could let y=0 represent the base of the tank and y=10 represent the top of the tank,
but we choose to keep the convention of the wording given in the problem and let y=0 represent ground level and hence y=-10 represents the bottom of the tank.
The actual height of the water does not matter;
rather, we are concerned with the distance the water travels.

