solution.p:
Again, as the pool is 20 wide,
this differential element represents a thin slice of water with volume V(y) = 20\cdot(5/3y+10)\cdot dy;
the height function is the same as before at h(y)=8-y.
The work performed in emptying this part of the pool is

  W_b = 62.4\int_0^3 20(5/3y+10)(8-y)\, dy = 299,520\,\text{ft--lb}
.

The total work in empyting the pool is

  W = W_b+W_t = 327,600+299,520 = 627,120\,\text{ft--lb}
.

