solution.p:
The differential equation we wish to solve is given by

  \frac{dy}{dt} = 6 - \frac{2y}{5}
.

The initial condition y(0) = 5 means that C = -10 so that

  y = 15 - 10e^{-\frac{2}{5}t}

is the particular solution to our initial value problem.

