li.p:
A sequence \{a_n\} is monotonically increasing
if a_n \leq a_{n+1} for all n, ,

  a_1 \leq a_2 \leq a_3 \leq \cdots a_n \leq a_{n+1} \cdots

A sequence \{a_n\} is monotonically decreasing
if a_n \geq a_{n+1} for all n, ,

  a_1 \geq a_2 \geq a_3 \geq \cdots a_n \geq a_{n+1} \cdots


  a_{n+1}-a_n \amp = \frac{n+2}{n+1} - \frac{n+1}{n}
  \amp = \frac{(n+2)(n)-(n+1)^2}{(n+1)n}
  \amp = \frac{-1}{n(n+1)}
  \amp \lt 0 \text{ for all \(n\). }

Since a_{n+1}-a_n\lt 0 for all n,
we conclude that the sequence is decreasing, illustrated in .

