\end{tikzpicture}

proof.p:
We begin by proving the formula for the simplied form for the partial sums.
Consider the nth partial sum of the geometric series,
S_n=\sum_{i=0}^n r^i:

  S_n \amp = 1+r+r^2+\cdots+r^{n-2}+r^{n-1}
  Multiply both sides by r:
  r\cdot S_n \amp = r+r^2+r^3+\dots+r^{n-1}+r^{n}
  Now subtract the second line from the first and solve for S_n:
  S_n-r\cdot S_n \amp = 1-r^n
  S_n(1-r) \amp = 1-r^{n}
  S_n \amp = \frac{1-r^{n}}{1-r}
.
We have shown Part
of .

