statement.p:
Find a rectangular equation for the curve described by

  x= \frac{1}{t^2+1} \text{ and }  y=\frac{t^2}{t^2+1}
.

solution.p:
Starting with x= 1/(t^2+1), solve for t:
t = \pm\sqrt{1/x-1}.
Substitute this value for t in the equation for y:

  y \amp = \frac{t^2}{t^2 +1}
  \amp = \frac{1/x-1}{1/x-1+1}
  \amp = \frac{1/x - 1}{1/x}
  \amp = \left(\frac1x-1\right)\cdot x
  \amp = 1-x
.

