li.p:
The equation r=1.5 describes all points that are 1.5 units from the pole;
as the angle is not specified,
any \theta is allowable.
All points 1.5 units from the pole describes a circle of radius 1.5.
We can consider the rectangular equivalent of this equation;
using r^2=x^2+y^2, we see that 1.5^2=x^2+y^2,
which we recognize as the equation of a circle centered at (0,0) with radius 1.5.
This is sketched in .

