section.p:
We rewrite the equation with parentheses to make a point:

  \vec v = \underbrace{\norm{\vec v}}_{\text{magnitude } }\cdot\underbrace{\left(\frac{1}{\norm{\vec v}}\vec v\right)}_{\text{direction } }
.

aside.p:
\vec 0 is directionless;
because \norm{\vec 0}=0,
there is no unit vector in the direction of \vec 0.

