section.p:
We can use to compute the dot product, but generally this theorem is used to find the angle between known vectors (since the dot product is generally easy to compute). To this end, we rewrite the theorem's equation as
\cos(	heta) =  rac{\dotp uv}{
orm{\vec u}
orm{\vec v}} \Leftrightarrow 	heta = \cos^{-1}\left( rac{\dotp uv}{
orm{\vec u}
orm{\vec v}}ight) .

