section.p:
We also know that \vec w is parallel to to \vec v; that is, the direction of \vec w is the direction of \vec v, described by the unit vector \vec v/
orm{\vec v}. The vector \vec w is the vector in the direction \vec v/
orm{\vec v} with magnitude 
orm{\vec u}\cos(	heta):
\vec w \amp = \Big(
orm{\vec u}\cos(	heta) \Big) rac{1}{
orm{\vec v}}\vec v \amp \amp \amp = \left(
orm{\vec u} rac{\dotp uv}{
orm{\vec u}
orm{\vec v}}ight) rac{1}{
orm{\vec v}} \vec v \amp \quad \amp 	ext{ (Replacing } \cos(	heta) 	ext{ using } 	ext{)} \amp =  rac{\dotp uv}{
orm{\vec v}^2}\vec v \amp \amp \amp =  rac{\dotp uv}{\dotp vv}\vec v \amp \amp 	ext{ (Applying }	ext{)} .

