solution.p:
Note how we did not actually compute the distance the object traveled,
nor the magnitude of the force in the direction of travel;
this is all inherently computed by the dot product!

By considering the sign of the dot product of the two vectors.
If the dot product is positive, the angle is acute;
if the dot product is negative, the angle is obtuse.

