solution.p:
At t=-1,
we have \vec v_1(-1) = \la 1,-2\ra and \vec v_2(-1) = \la 3,-6\ra;
the velocity of Object 2 is three times that of Object 1 and so it follows that the speed of Object 2 is three times that of Object 1 (3\sqrt{5} ft/s compared to \sqrt{5} ft/s.)

