solution.p:
The speed of the object is \norm{\vvt} = \sqrt{(-\sin(t) )^2+\cos^2(t) +1} = \sqrt{2}
;
it moves at a constant speed.
Note that the object does not accelerate in the z-direction,
but rather moves up at a constant rate of 1.

