subsection.p:
Likewise, given position function \vrt,
the average velocity on [a,b] is

  \frac{\text{displacement}}{\text{travel time}}\, = \frac1{b-a}\int_a^b \vec{r}\,'(t)\, dt = \frac{\vec r(b)-\vec r(a)}{b-a}
;
that is, it is the average value of \vrp(t),
or \vvt, on [a,b].

