statement.p:
The partial derivative of f with respect to x is:

  f_x(x,y,z) = \lim_{h\to 0} \frac{f(x+h,y,z)-f(x,y,z)}{h}
.

subsection.p:
We can continue taking partial derivatives of partial derivatives of partial derivatives of ;
we do not have to stop with second partial derivatives.
These higher order partial derivatives do not have a tidy graphical interpretation;
nevertheless they are not hard to compute and worthy of some practice.
    partial derivativehigh order

li.p:
To find f_{xyz}, we find f_x,
then f_{xy}, then f_{xyz}:

  f_x(x,y,z) \amp = 3x^2e^{xy}+ x^3ye^{xy}
  f_{xy}(x,y,z) \amp= 3x^3e^{xy}+x^3e^{xy}+x^4ye^{xy}
   \amp = 4x^3e^{xy}+x^4ye^{xy}
  f_{xyz}(x,y,z) \amp = 0
.

