introduction.p:
One can represent the terrain as the surface defined by a multivariable function f(x,y);
one can represent the path of the off-road vehicle, as seen from above,
with a vector-valued function \vec r(t) = \langle x(t),
y(t)\rangle;
the velocity of the vehicle is thus \vrp(t) = \langle x'(t),\yp(t)\rangle.

