solution.p:
We find that

  \frac{dz}{dt} = -\frac{2\cos^2(t) \sin(t) }{(1+\sin^2(t) )^2}-\frac{\sin(t) }{1+\sin^2(t) }
.

Using the angle sum/difference formula for tangent, we know

  \tan(2\pi t) = \tan(\pi t + \pi t) = \frac{\tan(\pi t)+\tan(\pi t)}{1-\tan^2(\pi t)}
.

Since the period of tangent is \pi,
we can adjust our answer to be

  \pi t = \pm\tan^{-1}(\sqrt{5})+ n\pi,\text{ where \(n\) is an integer. }

