solution.p:
This implies

  -2cx = \frac{dx}{dt}  \text{ and }    -4cy =\frac{dy}{dt}, \text{i.e.,}


  c = -\frac{1}{2x}\frac{dx}{dt}  \text{ and }    c =-\frac{1}{4y}\frac{dy}{dt}
.

As c equals both expressions, we have

  \frac{1}{2x}\frac{dx}{dt} =\frac{1}{4y}\frac{dy}{dt}
.

