solution.p:
A partial derivative is essentially a special case of a directional derivative;
it is the directional derivative in the direction of x or y,
, \la 1,0\ra or \la 0,1\ra.

\nabla f = \la 2x-y-7,4y-x\ra;
\nabla f(4,1) = \la 0,0\ra.
Since the gradient is zero, so is the directional derivative.

\nabla f = \la 2x-y-7,4y-x\ra;
\nabla f(4,1) = \la 0,0\ra.
Since the gradient is zero, so is the directional derivative.

