description.p:
The same bumpy surface as  is shown.
This time, we see a curve that lies in the surface;
the curve lies above the line x+y=\pi in the xy plane,
and passes through the same point as in the previous image.
The tangent line to the curve at this point is plotted;
it is the line tangent to the surface at (\pi/2, \pi/2) in the direction of \langle -1, 1\rangle.

