solution.p:
One critical point at (-4,2);
f_{xx} = 1 and D = 4,
so this point corresponds to a relative minimum.

Two critical points: at (0,-1);
f_{xx} = 2 and D = -12,
so this point corresponds to a saddle point;

Both f_x and f_y are undefined along the circle (x-3)^2+y^2=16;
at any point along this curve,
f(x,y)=0, the absolute minimum of the function.

