statement.p:
f(x,y) = 4;
R is the region enclosed by the petal of the rose curve
r=\sin(2\theta) in the first quadrant.

f(x,y) = \ln(x^2+y^2);
R is the annulus enclosed by the circles
x^2+y^2=1 and x^2+y^2=4.

f(x,y) = x^2-y^2;
R is the region enclosed by the circle
x^2+y^2=36 in the first and fourth quadrants.

f(x,y) = (x-y)/(x+y);
R is the region enclosed by the lines y=x,
y=0 and the circle x^2+y^2=1 in the first quadrant.

