solution.p:
The main point of this example is this:
integrating with respect to z first is rather straightforward;
integrating with respect to x first is not.

Collapsing D onto the xz-plane gives the region shown in ;
the lower curve is from the cylinder,
with equation z=2x^2+2.
The upper curve is from the paraboloid;
with y=0, the curve is z=6-2x^2.
Thus bounds on z are 2x^2+2\leq z\leq 6-2x^2;
the bounds on x are -1\leq x\leq 1.
Thus we have:

