solution.p:
Thus the mass is

  M = \oint_C \delta(s)\, ds = \int_0^{2\pi} \big(2+\sin(t)+\sin(2t)\big)\sqrt{1+4\cos^2(2t)}\, dt \approx 21.08\text{ gm }
.

statement.p:
C is the piecewise curve composed of the line segments that connect (0,1) to (1,1),
then connect (1,1) to (1,0);
the function is f(x,y)=x+y^2.

C: \vec r(t) = \langle t-t^2,t^2-t^3,t^3-t^4\rangle for 0\leq t\leq 1;
\delta(x,y,z) = x+2y+2z.
Use technology to approximate the value of each integral.

