statement.p:
Let \vec F be a vector field and let C be a curve.
Flow is a measure of the amount of \vec F going  C;
flux is a measure of the amount of \vec F going  C.

\vec F = \langle x-y,x+y\rangle;
C is the closed curve composed of the parabola y=x^2 on
0\leq x\leq 2 followed by the line segment from (2,4) to (0,0).

\vec F = \langle 0,x^2\rangle;
C the triangle with corners at (0,0),
(2,0) and (1,1).

\vec F = \langle x-y,x+y\rangle;
C is the closed curve composed of the parabola y=x^2 on
0\leq x\leq 2 followed by the line segment from (2,4) to (0,0).

\vec F = \langle 0,y^2\rangle;
C the triangle with corners at (0,0),
(2,0) and (1,1).

