subsection.p:
We now take the limit as n\to\infty, forcing \Delta u and \Delta v to 0. As \Delta u\to 0,
\frac{\vec r(u_i+\Delta u,v_j) - \vec r(u_i,v_j)}{\Delta u} \to \vec r_u(u_i,v_j) \text{ and }
\frac{\vec r(u_i,v_j+\Delta v)-\vec r(u_i,v_j)}{\Delta v} \to \vec r_v(u_i,v_j) .

answer.p:
Answers may vary;
one solution is \vec r(u,v) = \langle v\cos(u), v, 4v\sin(u)\rangle with
0\leq u\leq 2\pi, -1\leq v\leq 5.

