introduction.p:
A closed curve C that is the boundary of a surface \surfaceS is given along with a vector field \vec F.
Verify Stokes' Theorem on C;
that is, show \oint_C \vec F\cdot d\vec r = \iint_\surfaceS\big(\curl \vec F\,\big)\cdot\vec n\, dS.

